E["npc:fallen-hero-of-the-horde"] = {t="npc",n="Fallen Hero of the Horde",z="swampofsorrows",s="At the southern road from the Swamp of Sorrows, the Fallen Hero of the Horde keeps watch. Regret and dishonor bind him there. He warns travelers of the Blasted Lands and seeks champions to free his tortured soldiers from demonic bondage.",h="At the southern road from the Swamp of Sorrows, the Fallen Hero of the Horde keeps watch.",sec={{t="A Tragic Command",b="In life, the orc warrior was a celebrated champion. He led a handpicked regiment sent to investigate the Blasted Lands and report on the Burning Legion. But his dispatch never arrived. The courier bound for Stonard was ambushed and slain by the Swamp Talker and his murlocs.\n\nWithout orders or reinforcements, the commander marched south into the shattered wastes to face the growing darkness. It was a fatal choice. Demonic forces overwhelmed his army, scattering and capturing his soldiers. Razelikh the Defiler then subjected them to horrific torment.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Failure",b="The Fallen Hero of the Horde was captured with his lieutenant, Kirith, and tortured in the Serpent's Coil. Their captors tore the souls from his surviving men. He escaped, but fatal wounds claimed him near the swamp's border. His spirit remains tethered to the threshold of the Blasted Lands.\n\nHis soldiers met a darker fate. Their soulless husks were bound to mystic stones as immortal thralls. Razelikh and his lieutenants, Archmage Allistarj, Lady Sevine, and Grol the Destroyer, divided them among themselves. The soul-binding stones must be shattered and their torment ended before the restless spirit can know peace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was the Fallen Hero in life?",a="In life, he was a veteran orc warrior chosen to lead a reconnaissance force into the Blasted Lands and assess the demonic threat. He escaped torture at the hands of Razelikh the Defiler, but died of grievous wounds. His spirit remains by the road out of the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"fallen hero identity","fallen hero name","who is the fallen hero"}},{q="Why is he haunting the border of the Blasted Lands?",a="The shame of losing his regiment and failing his mission binds him to the border. He will not pass on until brave adventurers go south and destroy the stones of binding that hold his soldiers in eternal servitude to the Burning Legion.",al={"why is he a ghost","fallen hero ghost","why is he here"}},{q="What happened to the orders he sent to Stonard?",a="The scout carrying his urgent report to Stonard was ambushed and killed by murlocs led by the Swamp Talker. With the report lost, no reinforcements came, and the hero advanced alone into the Blasted Lands.",al={"missing orders","what happened to his orders","swamp talker courier"}},{q="What happened to his lieutenant, Kirith?",a="Lieutenant Kirith endured demonic experiments within the Serpent's Coil. His soul was warped, and his body became a monstrous felhunter lurking in the cave's depths.",al={"lieutenant kirith","who is kirith","what happened to kirith"},sp=1},{q="Why are his soldiers invulnerable?",a="Razelikh and his lieutenants severed the captive soldiers' souls from their flesh. Their soulless bodies cannot truly die. They can be freed only by battering the bodies near disintegration, which briefly leaves the nearby soul-binding stones vulnerable to destruction.",al={"invulnerable soldiers","stones of binding","servants of razelikh"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The hero shows the agony of a warrior whose honor demonic cruelty stripped away. As a Horde adventurer, you can avenge his lost squad and cleanse the stain of defeat from their legacy.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you may feel kinship with this fallen champion and understand the sting of surviving when comrades have fallen."},kw={"allistarj","fallen hero of the horde","grol the destroyer","lieutenant kirith","razelikh the defiler","sevine","stones of binding","swamp talker"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:blastedlands","subzone:serpent-s-coil","subzone:stonard","subzone:dark-portal","topic:burning-legion","topic:horde","topic:murloc"},src={"Fallen Hero of the Horde"}}
E["npc:fel-zerul"] = {t="npc",n="Fel'zerul",z="swampofsorrows",s="At Stonard, Fel'zerul watches the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar for danger. Thrall has sent him to learn what stirs there.",h="At Stonard, Fel'zerul watches the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar for danger.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Sunken Temple",b="From Stonard, Fel'zerul watches the corruption around the Pool of Tears and the submerged Temple of Atal'Hakkar. Thrall's Horde is wary of dark arts, yet the Warchief knows their students can help uncover the dangers they hold. So Fel'zerul directs adventurers to recover artifacts and investigate the exiled Atal'ai trolls. He seeks to learn what evil stirs beneath the waters before it threatens the Horde's southern outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fel'zerul?",a="Fel'zerul is an orc warlock living in Stonard, the Horde's stronghold in the Swamp of Sorrows. He investigates the dark rituals at the nearby Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",al={"felzerul","who is fel'zerul","stonard warlock"}},{q="Why did Thrall send a warlock to Stonard?",a="Warchief Thrall sent Fel'zerul to Stonard because ancient curses and blood rituals call for knowledge of dark sorceries. Fel'zerul watches the sunken temple and works to protect Horde interests in the swamp.",al={"thrall felzerul","why is felzerul here","felzerul mission"}},{q="What is Fel'zerul investigating?",a="Fel'zerul investigates the Atal'ai trolls and their rites at the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, by the Pool of Tears. He sends scouts and adventurers to recover artifacts and seek exiled priests who may know its lore.",al={"felzerul quest lore","what does felzerul want","pool of tears investigation"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, Fel'zerul shows that Thrall's new Horde sometimes relies on practitioners of the dark arts to face obscure, esoteric threats.",["faction:Horde"]="At Stonard, Fel'zerul watches for dark magic in the swamp, helping guard the Horde's foothold in the region."},kw={"atal'hakkar","fel'zerul","felzerul","stonard","swamp of sorrows","thrall","warlock"},rel={"subzone:stonard","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:pool-of-tears","zone:swampofsorrows","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Fel'zerul"}}
E["quest:1389"] = {t="quest",n="Draenethyst Crystals",z="swampofsorrows",s="At the Harborage, Magtoor asks you to recover six draenethyst crystals stolen from the Fallow Sanctuary. Sacred to his people, the crystals are bound to their fear of losing their way.",h="At the Harborage, Magtoor asks you to recover six draenethyst crystals stolen from the Fallow Sanctuary.",sec={{t="The Lost Ones",b="The lost ones of the Fallow Sanctuary resemble Magtoor's people. The journey to Azeroth drove them mad. Once brethren, they now dwell in the Sanctuary to the east, where they seize or kill anyone who strays close. They have also stolen draenethyst crystals, sacred to Magtoor's people.",sp=0},{t="Without the Crystals",b="Magtoor's people lack the strength to enter the Fallow Sanctuary and reclaim the draenethyst among its huts and campfires. Without the crystals, they fear they too may lose their way. So Magtoor asks you to bring back six.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the draenethyst crystals?",a="Magtoor asks for the crystals from the Harborage.",al={"who gives draenethyst crystals","magtoor quest","who wants draenethyst"}},{q="Why are the draenethyst crystals important to Magtoor?",a="The draenethyst crystals are sacred to Magtoor's people. Without them, Magtoor fears they too may lose their way.",al={"why draenethyst crystals","what do draenethyst crystals do","draenethyst purpose"}},{q="Who took the crystals?",a="The lost ones of the Fallow Sanctuary took the crystals. They were once Magtoor's brethren, until the rigors of the journey to Azeroth drove them mad.",al={"who stole draenethyst","who has the crystals","fallow sanctuary enemies"}},{q="Where can the crystals be found?",a="You can find the crystals among the huts and campfires of the Fallow Sanctuary, to the east.",al={"draenethyst crystal location","where are draenethyst crystals","find draenethyst"}},{q="Why can't Magtoor's people retrieve them themselves?",a="Magtoor's people lack the strength to enter the Sanctuary and take the crystals back.",al={"why doesn't magtoor fight","why help magtoor"}}},kw={"draenethyst","fallow sanctuary","harborage","lost ones","magtoor","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"subzone:harborage","subzone:fallow-sanctuary","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Magtoor",["end"]="Magtoor",level="35",id=1389},src={"Draenethyst Crystals (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1392"] = {t="quest",n="Noboru the Cudgel",z="swampofsorrows",s="At the Harborage, the Draenei have endured Noboru the Cudgel’s torment for months. You carry his cudgel to their leader, a token of the cruelty the lost ones have dealt them.",h="At the Harborage, the Draenei have endured Noboru the Cudgel’s torment for months.",sec={{t="A Symbol of Brutality",b="For months, Noboru has tormented the Draenei who live at the Harborage. His cudgel recalls the cruelty the lost ones have dealt them. You carry it to their leader.",sp=0},{t="Magtoor's Welcome",b="Magtoor asks whether the weapon means Noboru is dead. He calls it a day of joy for the Harborage. Noboru and his gang terrorized the Draenei as they wandered the swamps, killing anyone who crossed their path. Noboru threatened their very survival, and they lacked the strength to face him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Noboru?",a="Noboru is one of the lost ones who has tormented the Harborage’s Draenei for months.",al={"who is noboru","noboru lore","noboru cudgel guy"}},{q="Why does the Harborage want Noboru's cudgel?",a="The cudgel recalls the cruelty the lost ones have dealt the Draenei of the Harborage.",al={"why turn in the cudgel","noboru cudgel purpose","why bring cudgel to magtoor"}},{q="Who receives the cudgel?",a="Magtoor, the leader of the Harborage, receives the cudgel.",al={"who is magtoor","where does the cudgel go"}},{q="Where is the Harborage located?",a="The Harborage is in the Swamp of Sorrows, where its Draenei live.",al={"where is harborage","harborage location"}}},kw={"cudgel","draenei","harborage","lost ones","magtoor","noboru","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:harborage"},m={start="Noboru's Cudgel",["end"]="Magtoor",level="39",faction="Neutral",id=1392},src={"Noboru the Cudgel (quest)"}}
E["quest:1393"] = {t="quest",n="Galen's Escape",z="swampofsorrows",s="In the Fallow Sanctuary, Galen Goodward calls for help as creatures close around him. He offers a great treasure from his camp north of Stonard.",h="In the Fallow Sanctuary, Galen Goodward calls for help as creatures close around him.",sec={{t="A Plea for Rescue",b="Galen Goodward calls out from the Fallow Sanctuary, afraid the creatures around him will eat him. He promises a great treasure to anyone who gets him out. It lies in a strongbox at his camp in the swamp north of Stonard. Only Galen knows the trick to open it, and he will teach it to whoever rescues him.",sp=0},{t="At the Strongbox",b="At Galen's camp, black resin blocks the strongbox's keyhole. Galen told you of a latch hidden beneath the box. You find it with a quick search, and flipping it opens the strongbox.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Galen Goodward?",a="Galen Goodward is held in the Fallow Sanctuary, where he fears the creatures will eat him. He offers a great treasure to anyone who helps him escape.",al={"who is galen","galen goodward lore","galens escape guy"}},{q="Where is Galen's camp located?",a="Galen's camp lies in the swamp north of Stonard, in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"where is galens camp","galens strongbox location","where is the strongbox"}},{q="Why can't the strongbox be opened in the usual way?",a="Black resin blocks the strongbox's keyhole, and Galen knows a hidden latch beneath it. He promises to teach the trick to anyone who helps him escape.",al={"how to open strongbox","galen chest key"}}},kw={"black resin","fallow sanctuary","galen goodward","galen's escape","stonard","strongbox","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"subzone:fallow-sanctuary","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:stonard"},m={start="Galen Goodward",["end"]="Galen's Strongbox",level="38",id=1393},src={"Galen's Escape"}}
E["quest:1396"] = {t="quest",n="Encroaching Wildlife",z="swampofsorrows",s="After Lost Ones wreck Watcher Biggs's caravan, wild creatures prowl near his camp. Biggs alone survives and asks you to help defend the supplies that remain. This follows Help Watcher Biggs.",h="After Lost Ones wreck Watcher Biggs's caravan, wild creatures prowl near his camp.",sec={{t="A Camp Under Watch",b="Watcher Biggs's caravan set out for the eastern coast, but never arrived. Lost Ones attacked, killing the guards and smashing the supplies. Biggs alone survived, and he has sworn to protect what remains. Now wild creatures skulk near the camp, and Biggs asks you to help defend it.",sp=0},{t="The Creatures Nearby",b="Young sawtooth crocolisks, sorrow spinners and swamp jaguars press close to the camp. Biggs names eight crocolisks, ten spinners and ten jaguars to be slain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where was Watcher Biggs's caravan traveling?",a="Watcher Biggs's caravan was bound for the eastern coast, but it never arrived.",al={"where was biggs going","caravan destination","biggs caravan route"}},{q="Who attacked Watcher Biggs's caravan?",a="Lost Ones attacked the caravan, killing the guards and smashing the supplies. Watcher Biggs alone survived.",al={"who attacked biggs","who destroyed the caravan","caravan ambush"}},{q="What beasts threaten the camp?",a="Young sawtooth crocolisks, sorrow spinners and swamp jaguars skulk near the camp.",al={"which beasts are encroaching","what animals attack biggs","swamp beasts"}},{q="Why does Watcher Biggs remain at the camp?",a="Watcher Biggs has sworn to protect the supplies that remain from the caravan.",al={"why is biggs staying","why not flee","biggs supplies"}}},kw={"caravan","lost ones","sawtooth crocolisk","sorrow spinner","supplies","swamp jaguar","swamp of sorrows","watcher biggs"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","quest:1421"},m={start="Watcher Biggs",["end"]="Watcher Biggs",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=1396},src={"Encroaching Wildlife"}}
E["quest:1398"] = {t="quest",n="Driftwood",z="swampofsorrows",s="Watcher Biggs sends you east to the coast for dry driftwood. He needs it to mend his wagon before he can reach Nethergarde.",h="Watcher Biggs sends you east to the coast for dry driftwood.",sec={{t="Wood for the Wagon",b="Watcher Biggs thanks you and asks for help again. His wagon needs repairs before he can reach Nethergarde. The swamp's wood is too spongy and tangled to use, so he needs strong, dry wood.",sp=0},{t="Driftwood from the Coast",b="Watcher Biggs sends you east to the coast for driftwood dried by the sun. Bring eight pieces back to him in the Swamp of Sorrows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Watcher Biggs need wood?",a="Biggs needs wood to mend his wagon so he can reach Nethergarde. The swamp's trees are too spongy and tangled.",al={"driftwood reason","why does biggs need driftwood","why driftwood"}},{q="Where does Watcher Biggs send you for the wood?",a="He sends you east to the coast for driftwood dried by the sun.",al={"driftwood location","where to find driftwood","where is the wood"}},{q="What came before this?",a="The Lost Caravan comes first. Biggs then asks you for more help.",al={"driftwood previous quest","what leads to driftwood","what quest comes before driftwood"}},{q="How much driftwood is needed?",a="Eight pieces of driftwood dried by the sun.",al={"driftwood count","how many driftwood"}},{q="What comes after gathering the driftwood?",a="Deliver the Shipment follows.",al={"driftwood follow up","what is after driftwood","driftwood next quest"}}},kw={"driftwood","nethergarde","sundried driftwood","swamp of sorrows","wagon","watcher biggs"},rel={"quest:1421","quest:1425","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Watcher Biggs",["end"]="Watcher Biggs",level="42",faction="Alliance",id=1398},src={"Driftwood (quest)"}}
E["quest:1418"] = {t="quest",n="Neeka Bloodscar",z="swampofsorrows",s="In Stonard, Helgrum the Swift sends you to Kargath, where his messages often fail to arrive.",h="In Stonard, Helgrum the Swift sends you to Kargath, where his messages often fail to arrive.",sec={{t="A Cut Line",b="In the Badlands, harsh country near Alliance-held Loch Modan, messages between Stonard and Kargath often fail. Helgrum asks you to prove yourself by traveling to Kargath and speaking with Neeka Bloodscar, its head scout. Then you carry Neeka's report back to Helgrum.",sp=0},{t="Neeka's Answer",b="Neeka Bloodscar tells you an outrunner left for Stonard barely three days ago. Since no word from Neeka has reached Stonard, the runner must have failed. Neeka hopes the next one has more skill or luck.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Helgrum the Swift send you?",a="Helgrum the Swift sends you from Stonard to Kargath, an outpost in the Badlands, to speak with its head scout, Neeka Bloodscar.",al={"where do i go","neeka bloodscar location","where is neeka"}},{q="Why is communication between Stonard and Kargath cut off?",a="The Badlands are harsh country near Loch Modan, which the Alliance holds. Messages between Stonard and Kargath often fail.",al={"why are communications cut","badlands communication problem","why stonard to kargath"}},{q="Who is Neeka Bloodscar?",a="Neeka Bloodscar is the head scout at the Kargath outpost in the Badlands.",al={"who is neeka","neeka role","neeka bloodscar lore"}},{q="What comes after speaking with Neeka Bloodscar?",a="After speaking with Neeka Bloodscar, you report back to Helgrum.",al={"what next","follow up quest","after neeka bloodscar"}}},kw={"badlands","head scout","helgrum the swift","kargath","loch modan","neeka bloodscar","stonard","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"subzone:kargath","subzone:stonard","zone:badlands","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:lochmodan","quest:1420","topic:alliance"},m={start="Helgrum the Swift",["end"]="Neeka Bloodscar",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1418},src={"Neeka Bloodscar (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1421"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Caravan",z="swampofsorrows",s="Watcher Biggs needs the caravan's reagents recovered after the Lost Ones carry a wagon north to the Fallow Sanctuary. The chest holds supplies for the wizards of Nethergarde Keep.",h="Watcher Biggs needs the caravan's reagents recovered after the Lost Ones carry a wagon north to the Fallow...",sec={{t="The Stolen Wagon",b="Watcher Biggs was knocked senseless when the Lost Ones attacked the caravan. Before he fell, he saw them drag one of its wagons north to the Fallow Sanctuary, their village. A chest of reagents was aboard, prized by the wizards of Nethergarde Keep for their studies. Biggs asks you to find the chest and carry its contents back.",sp=0},{t="Word from Biggs",b="When you bring the reagents back, Watcher Biggs is pleased. The wizards of Nethergarde can continue their work, though Biggs does not know what that work is. He knows it concerns the Dark Portal in the Blasted Lands and matters greatly to the Alliance's security.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Watcher Biggs?",a="Watcher Biggs lost one of the caravan's wagons to the Lost Ones and wants its reagents recovered.",al={"watcher biggs","who gives the lost caravan"}},{q="Where did the Lost Ones take the caravan chest?",a="Watcher Biggs saw the wagon hauled north to the Fallow Sanctuary, the Lost Ones' village, with the chest aboard.",al={"caravan chest location","where is fallow sanctuary","where are the reagents"}},{q="Why are the reagents important?",a="The wizards of Nethergarde Keep depend on the reagents for their studies.",al={"why reagents matter","nethergarde reagents purpose"}},{q="What comes after recovering the chest?",a="Driftwood follows once Watcher Biggs has the reagents.",al={"next quest after lost caravan","lost caravan chain"}}},kw={"dark portal","fallow sanctuary","lost ones","nethergarde keep","swamp of sorrows","watcher biggs","wizards reagents"},rel={"subzone:fallow-sanctuary","subzone:nethergarde-keep","quest:1396","subzone:dark-portal","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:blastedlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Watcher Biggs",["end"]="Watcher Biggs",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1421},src={"The Lost Caravan"}}
E["quest:1422"] = {t="quest",n="Threat From the Sea",z="swampofsorrows",s="Tok'Kar works on your weapon while Katar reports the beach patrols could use help.",h="Tok'Kar works on your weapon while Katar reports the beach patrols could use help.",sec={{t="A Word with Katar",b="Tok'Kar works on your weapon and sends you to Katar. Katar says the beach patrols could use help. Some louses at camp drink, but Tok'Kar would rather you keep your wits sharp and your weapons ready than join them.",sp=0},{t="Over the Roar of the Sea",b="Katar asks you for a moment of silence. Over the sea's dull roar, you can hear the fish men's disgusting gurgling.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Tok'Kar send you to Katar?",a="Tok'Kar is busy with your weapon, so he sends you to Katar and wants you to keep your wits and weapons ready instead of drinking with the louses at camp.",al={"why talk to katar","tok'kar reason","why visit katar"}},{q="What does Katar need assistance with?",a="Katar says the patrols along the beach could use some help.",al={"katar problem","what does katar want","katar patrol"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="After Lack of Surplus, Tok'Kar begins work on your weapon.",al={"previous quest","prereq","threat from the sea chain"}}},kw={"beach","katar","patrol","shore","swamp of sorrows","threat from the sea","tok'kar"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Tok'Kar",["end"]="Katar",level="45",faction="Horde",id=1422},src={"Threat From the Sea"}}
E["quest:1423"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Supplies",z="swampofsorrows",s="A barrel bound for Nethergarde Keep bears Quartermaster Lungertz’s name.",h="A barrel bound for Nethergarde Keep bears Quartermaster Lungertz’s name.",sec={{t="A Stamped Barrel",b="Pungent yellow wax seals the seams of a small, sturdy barrel. Its base carries a stamp naming Quartermaster Lungertz and Nethergarde Keep, marking where it belongs.",sp=0},{t="Word from the Quartermaster",b="Quartermaster Lungertz thanks you for the recovered supplies. They often go astray on the road from Darkshire to Nethergarde. Some have now been found.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is meant to receive the lost supplies?",a="The barrel is marked for Quartermaster Lungertz at Nethergarde Keep.",al={"who gets the barrel","lost supplies recipient","where does the barrel go"}},{q="How can you tell who owns the barrel?",a="A stamp on the barrel’s base names Quartermaster Lungertz and Nethergarde Keep.",al={"barrel markings","how to read barrel","quartermaster lungertz stamp"}},{q="What does the barrel look like?",a="It is a small, sturdy barrel with pungent yellow wax sealing its seams.",al={"lost supplies barrel","barrel description"}}},kw={"barrel","darkshire","lost supplies","nethergarde keep","quartermaster lungertz","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:darkshire"},m={start="Lost Supplies (starter)",["end"]="Quartermaster Lungertz",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=1423},src={"The Lost Supplies"}}
E["quest:1424"] = {t="quest",n="Pool of Tears",z="swampofsorrows",s="In Stonard, Fel'zerul sends you to search the Pool of Tears for Atal'ai artifacts. The Warchief's people came to investigate strange events at the Temple of Atal'Hakkar and found it sunk.",h="In Stonard, Fel'zerul sends you to search the Pool of Tears for Atal'ai artifacts.",sec={{t="The Sunken Temple",b="The Atal'ai trolls are a tribe of dark casters known for forbidden magic. Fel'zerul's party reached the Temple of Atal'Hakkar and found it sunk. Green dragons now watch over the temple and call themselves protectors of Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Pieces of a Puzzle",b="Fel'zerul wants to learn what happened, so he asks you to gather Atal'ai artifacts around the Pool of Tears. The pieces may help the puzzle come together. No one knows what dark rites the trolls practiced in the temple, only that they used great magical forces. Fel'zerul hopes their spells may aid the Horde. He wants to learn what the Atal'ai sought and what went so horribly wrong.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fel'zerul?",a="Fel'zerul is in Stonard, among those the Warchief sent to investigate strange events at the Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",al={"fel'zerul","felzerul","who gives pool of tears"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in the Atal'ai trolls?",a="Fel'zerul says great magical forces were used at the temple. He hopes the Atal'ai's spells may prove useful to the Horde.",al={"why horde wants atal'ai","atal'ai magic horde"}},{q="Where are the Atal'ai artifacts located?",a="The Atal'ai artifacts lie on the bed of the Pool of Tears, near the temple.",al={"atal'ai artifact location","where to find artifacts","pool of tears artifacts"}},{q="Who guards the sunken temple now?",a="Green dragons watch over the sunken temple and call themselves protectors of Azeroth.",al={"why are green dragons here","green dragons temple of atal'hakkar","green dragons swamp of sorrows"}},{q="What comes next after the artifacts are delivered?",a="The Atal'ai Exile follows.",al={"next quest after pool of tears","pool of tears follow up","what after pool of tears"}}},kw={"artifacts","atal'ai","fel'zerul","green dragons","pool of tears","stonard","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar","warchief"},rel={"subzone:pool-of-tears","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:stonard","npc:fel-zerul","quest:1429","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:horde","topic:troll"},m={start="Fel'zerul",["end"]="Fel'zerul",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1424},src={"Pool of Tears (Horde)"}}
E["quest:1425"] = {t="quest",n="Deliver the Shipment",z="swampofsorrows",s="After Driftwood, Watcher Biggs asks you to carry supplies to Quartermaster Lungertz at Nethergarde Keep while his wagon is repaired.",h="After Driftwood, Watcher Biggs asks you to carry supplies to Quartermaster Lungertz at Nethergarde Keep while...",sec={{t="A Last Delivery for Biggs",b="Watcher Biggs packs the key supplies rescued from the ogre attacks for you to carry. He stays behind to repair the wagon. Nethergarde Keep lies in the Blasted Lands' northern hills and watches over the Dark Portal. Biggs sends you east along the road, then south into the Blasted Lands where it branches. At the next fork, take the left turn and stay wary.",sp=0},{t="At Nethergarde",b="Quartermaster Lungertz is startled when you arrive with a package from Biggs' caravan. The keep had given up the caravan and Biggs for lost. Lungertz thanks you and hopes the supplies include Azoran Crystals, a reagent the keep badly needs and is running low on.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends the shipment to Nethergarde?",a="Watcher Biggs packed the key supplies rescued from the ogre attacks while he stays behind to repair the wagon.",al={"who gives deliver the shipment","deliver the shipment quest giver","watcher biggs delivery"}},{q="Where does this shipment need to go?",a="You carry the supplies to Quartermaster Lungertz at Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands' northern hills.",al={"where is nethergarde keep","how to get to nethergarde","quartermaster lungertz location"}},{q="What comes directly before this delivery?",a="This delivery follows Driftwood.",al={"deliver the shipment prerequisite","what quest comes before deliver the shipment"}},{q="What route leads from the swamp to the keep?",a="Follow the road east, then turn south into the Blasted Lands where it branches. At the next fork, take the left turn.",al={"directions to nethergarde keep","path to blasted lands"}},{q="What is Nethergarde Keep watching over?",a="Nethergarde Keep watches over the Dark Portal.",al={"purpose of nethergarde keep","why is nethergarde in blasted lands"}}},kw={"azoran crystals","blasted lands","dark portal","nethergarde keep","quartermaster lungertz","shipment","swamp of sorrows","watcher biggs"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:dark-portal"},m={start="Watcher Biggs",["end"]="Quartermaster Lungertz",level="42",faction="Alliance",id=1425},src={"Deliver the Shipment"}}
E["quest:1426"] = {t="quest",n="Threat From the Sea",z="swampofsorrows",s="Tok'Kar sends you to Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows. Katar hates the sea and takes pleasure in seeing fish men fall to those who serve the Horde. Now Katar asks how many you can slay and whether you can face their strongest kind.",h="Tok'Kar sends you to Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Grudge Against the Sea",b="In the Swamp of Sorrows, Katar asks you to kill marsh murlocs, marsh inkspewers and marsh flesheaters. Katar despises the sea and every creature from it. To Katar, the sea is a strong but blind, callous and brutal mistress. Slaying fish men by the hundreds would delight Katar, if that were possible. For now, watching them fall to those who serve the Horde brings some satisfaction.",sp=0},{t="Katar's Verdict",b="When you return, Katar says the sea may seem vast and relentless, yet its offspring now bear your bloody mark. The fish men know pain and must rebuild their ranks, which pleases Katar. Each time one is silenced, Katar will smile and invite you to slay more.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Katar want the murlocs destroyed?",a="Katar hates the sea and every creature from it, and would gladly see fish men slain by the hundreds. Watching them die at the hands of those who serve the Horde gives Katar some pleasure.",al={"why kill murlocs","katar murlocs","why hate sea"}},{q="Where does this hunt take place?",a="You hunt marsh murlocs, marsh inkspewers and marsh flesheaters in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"where are the marsh murlocs","threat from the sea location"}},{q="Who gives this hunt?",a="Katar gives the hunt in the Swamp of Sorrows, after Tok'Kar sends you to speak with Katar.",al={"who gives threat from the sea","threat from the sea questgiver"}},{q="What comes before this hunt?",a="It follows the first Threat From the Sea, when Tok'Kar sent you to speak with Katar.",al={"threat from the sea prerequisite","threat from the sea previous quest"}}},kw={"katar","marsh flesheater","marsh inkspewer","marsh murloc","murloc","swamp of sorrows","threat from the sea"},rel={"quest:1422","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc","topic:horde"},m={start="Katar",["end"]="Katar",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1426},src={"Threat From the Sea (2)"}}
E["quest:1427"] = {t="quest",n="Threat From the Sea",z="swampofsorrows",s="Katar sends you back to Tok'Kar before you rest. He believes Tok'Kar finished a few weapons while you were away, and one will be offered to you for your help.",h="Katar sends you back to Tok'Kar before you rest.",sec={{t="Back to Tok'Kar",b="Before you rest, Katar sends you back to Tok'Kar. He believes Tok'Kar finished a few weapons while you were away. Tok'Kar will offer you one for your help. Katar says you could test its strength against the murlocs when ready, which would please him further.",sp=0},{t="Tok'Kar's Thanks",b="Tok'Kar is glad to see you return. More weapons have been made for the war on the murlocs. In thanks for bringing fresh sawtooth meat and putting a small smile on Katar's face, he gives you one.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Tok'Kar?",a="Katar sends you to speak with Tok'Kar once more before you rest in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"who gives this quest","where do I get threat from the sea","who starts this"}},{q="Why is Tok'Kar offering a weapon?",a="Katar believes Tok'Kar finished a few weapons while you were away, and will offer you one in thanks for your help.",al={"why does tok'kar give a weapon","what did tok'kar make","tok'kar reward reason"}},{q="What comes next after speaking with Tok'Kar?",a="Continued Threat follows.",al={"what is the next quest","where to after this","what follows threat from the sea"}}},kw={"katar","murloc","sawtooth meat","swamp of sorrows","threat from the sea","tok'kar"},rel={"quest:1428","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc"},m={start="Katar",["end"]="Tok'Kar",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1427},src={"Threat From the Sea (3)"}}
E["quest:1428"] = {t="quest",n="Continued Threat",z="swampofsorrows",s="Along the Swamp of Sorrows beach, Katar sees your hatred of the fish men growing like her own.",h="Along the Swamp of Sorrows beach, Katar sees your hatred of the fish men growing like her own.",sec={{t="More Along the Beach",b="Katar sends you farther along the beach to hunt marsh inkspewers, marsh flesheaters and marsh oracles. Return when you have had enough of the fight. She will take no pleasure until the sea and all her children are silenced, with the repulsive fish men foremost in her thoughts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Katar gives you this work on the Swamp of Sorrows beach.",al={"who starts continued threat","continued threat quest giver","katar swamp of sorrows"}},{q="What creatures need to be hunted?",a="Katar wants you to hunt marsh inkspewers, marsh flesheaters and marsh oracles along the beach.",al={"what to kill continued threat","continued threat targets","which murlocs"}},{q="Why does Katar want the murlocs culled?",a="Katar will take no pleasure until the sea and her brood are silenced, especially the fish men.",al={"why kill murlocs","katar motive","why hate fish men"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="This follows Threat From the Sea, after which Tok'Kar offered you a weapon.",al={"continued threat prerequisite","previous quest continued threat"}}},kw={"continued threat","fish men","katar","marsh flesheater","marsh inkspewer","marsh oracle","murlocs","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Katar",["end"]="Katar",level="45",faction="Horde",id=1428},src={"Continued Threat"}}
E["quest:1429"] = {t="quest",n="The Atal'ai Exile",z="swampofsorrows",s="At Stonard, Fel'zerul sends you north with the artifacts from the Pool of Tears. Find an exiled Atal'ai priest in the Hinterlands and learn what the artifacts are for.",h="At Stonard, Fel'zerul sends you north with the artifacts from the Pool of Tears.",sec={{t="A Sentence in Blood",b="A blood-marked scroll sentences an Atal'ai priest to a fate worse than death among his own people. He is sent to live with the Witherbark trolls, far north in the Hinterlands. Fel'zerul bundles the artifacts and sends you to find the exile, learn their true use, and return.",sp=0},{t="The Exile's Words",b="The Atal'ai exile names the artifacts as tools for summoning when shown the bundle. He says Jammal'an the Prophet is leading the disciples of the Chamber of Blood toward their chosen fate. The exile wonders whether Hakkar has returned to the temple.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find the Atal'ai Exile?",a="Fel'zerul in Stonard sends you north with the artifacts you gathered.",al={"who gives the atal'ai exile","atal'ai exile questgiver","who starts the quest"}},{q="Where is the Atal'ai Exile located?",a="The Atal'ai Exile lives with the Witherbark trolls at the temple of Shadra'Alor in the Hinterlands.",al={"where is the exile","atal'ai exile location","where to find atal'ai exile"}},{q="What sentence was passed on the priest?",a="A blood-marked scroll sentences the priest to exile among the Witherbark trolls in the Hinterlands, a fate worse than death among the Atal'ai.",al={"why was he banished","what was the sentence","atal'ai exile backstory"}},{q="What are you carrying to the exile?",a="You carry Atal'ai artifacts gathered at the Pool of Tears. Fel'zerul wants the exile to reveal their true use.",al={"what bundle do you bring","what are the artifacts","atal'ai artifacts purpose"}},{q="What comes directly before this journey?",a="Your journey follows Pool of Tears, where Fel'zerul had you gather Atal'ai artifacts.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","what leads to atal'ai exile"}}},kw={"atal'ai exile","fel'zerul","hakkar","hinterlands","jammal'an","pool of tears","shadra'alor","swamp of sorrows","witherbark"},rel={"npc:fel-zerul","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:hinterlands","subzone:pool-of-tears","topic:troll","topic:priest"},m={start="Fel'zerul",["end"]="Atal'ai Exile",level="44",faction="Horde",id=1429},src={"The Atal'ai Exile"}}
E["quest:1430"] = {t="quest",n="Fresh Meat",z="swampofsorrows",s="Dar needs crawler legs from the coast for hungry customers in Orgrimmar.",h="Dar needs crawler legs from the coast for hungry customers in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Crawler Legs for Orgrimmar",b="Dar's customers in Orgrimmar crave crawler meat, especially from the monstrous crawlers. East of here, the creatures scurry over the beaches and into the surf. Bring back some of their legs, and Dar promises a cask of wine. He means to taste the meat before it goes on to Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="A Taste for the Road",b="Dar is pleased with the legs and pictures them cooked over an open fire. He urges you to take a cooked sample on your travels. Dar swears it is delicious.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wants crawler meat in the Swamp of Sorrows?",a="Dar's customers in Orgrimmar have a high demand for crawler meat.",al={"who gives fresh meat","dar quest","who is dar"}},{q="Where are the monstrous crawlers located?",a="The monstrous crawlers scurry along the coast to the east, over the beaches and into the surf.",al={"crawler location","where are the crawlers","monstrous crawler shore"}},{q="Why does Dar need these specific legs?",a="Dar's customers crave crawler meat, especially from the monstrous crawlers. The legs are bound for Orgrimmar.",al={"why crawler meat","what is the meat for","orgrimmar crawler meat"}}},kw={"crawler legs","dar","fresh meat","monstrous crawler","orgrimmar","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:orgrimmar","item:crawler-leg"},m={start="Dar",["end"]="Dar",level="44",faction="Horde",id=1430},src={"Fresh Meat (Swamp of Sorrows)"}}
E["quest:2622"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Orders",z="swampofsorrows",s="Dispatch Commander Ruag sends you to find Bengor after the orders go missing.",h="Dispatch Commander Ruag sends you to find Bengor after the orders go missing.",sec={{t="Ruag's Account",b="Dispatch Commander Ruag bristles when you ask about the missing orders. He says they went with the soldiers sent to carry them. Murlocs ambushed and brutally beat the soldiers, and only one survived. Bengor can barely speak, cannot walk, and is fed through a tube. Ruag sends you to find him nearby, then warns you to mind what you poke your nose into.",sp=0},{t="Bengor's Halting Words",b="Bengor can manage only broken scraps of speech. Among them, you catch the words swamp talker.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sent the orders that went missing?",a="Dispatch Commander Ruag says the orders went with the soldiers sent out. He grows defensive when you ask what became of them.",al={"who gave missing orders","who lost the orders"}},{q="What happened to the soldiers carrying the orders?",a="Dispatch Commander Ruag says murlocs ambushed and brutally beat the soldiers carrying the orders. Only one survived.",al={"what happened to couriers","how were the orders lost"}},{q="Who is Bengor?",a="Bengor is the sole survivor of the ambush. He can barely speak, cannot walk, and is fed through a tube.",al={"who is the survivor","bengor lore"}},{q="Where can Bengor be found?",a="Dispatch Commander Ruag says Bengor is somewhere nearby.",al={"bengor location","where is bengor"}}},kw={"ambush","bengor","dispatch commander ruag","missing orders","murloc","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"quest:2623","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc"},m={start="Dispatch Commander Ruag",["end"]="Bengor",level="50",faction="Horde",id=2622},src={"The Missing Orders"}}
E["quest:2623"] = {t="quest",n="The Swamp Talker",z="swampofsorrows",s="Orders bound for the Blasted Lands vanish in a murloc ambush. Bengor tells you what happened before he loses consciousness.",h="Orders bound for the Blasted Lands vanish in a murloc ambush.",sec={{t="Bengor's Broken Account",b="Bengor says the dispatch commander gave out the orders. His group was bound for the Blasted Lands when many murlocs fell upon them. One of them, Swamp Talker, seized the orders from Bengor as a spear struck his skull. Before he passes out, Bengor speaks of a cave to the east. Recover the orders and take them to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Hero's Reckoning",b="The Fallen Hero of the Horde finds the cost worse than imagined. Nineteen of the Hero's men might have been spared agony if the Hero had not acted so irrationally. Powerless to help them, the Hero asks you to aid those men.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who stole the Warchief's Orders?",a="During the ambush, a murloc named Swamp Talker took the orders from Bengor's hands.",al={"who took the orders","who is swamp talker","who stole orders"}},{q="Where did the Swamp Talker go?",a="As Bengor fades, he speaks of a cave to the east.",al={"where is swamp talker","swamp talker location","where is the murloc cave"}},{q="Where were Bengor and his unit heading?",a="Bengor and his unit were carrying orders from the dispatch commander to the Blasted Lands when murlocs ambushed them.",al={"bengor destination","where was bengor going","bengor unit goal"}},{q="To whom should the orders be returned?",a="Take the orders to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.",al={"who gets the warchief orders","where do i turn in the orders","turn in swamp talker quest"}}},kw={"bengor","blasted lands","fallen hero of the horde","murloc","swamp of sorrows","swamp talker","warchief's orders"},rel={"quest:2622","npc:fallen-hero-of-the-horde","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:blastedlands","topic:murloc","topic:horde"},m={start="Bengor",["end"]="Fallen Hero of the Horde",level="55",faction="Horde",id=2623},src={"The Swamp Talker"}}
E["quest:3374"] = {t="quest",n="The Essence of Eranikus",z="swampofsorrows",s="At the Oathstone, Itharius reaches you through the stone and asks you to help redeem Eranikus's corrupted soul. The first sacrifice is the gem that chains the free part of Eranikus's mind. Itharius waits in the Swamp of Sorrows.",h="At the Oathstone, Itharius reaches you through the stone and asks you to help redeem Eranikus's corrupted...",sec={{t="A Voice Through the Stone",b="Through the Oathstone, Itharius asks you to aid Ysera's Dragonflight in redeeming Eranikus's corrupted soul. He warns that many sacrifices will be asked of you both. First, give him the gem that chains the part of Eranikus's mind still free. Take the Oathstone and the Chained Essence of Eranikus to Itharius in the Swamp of Sorrows. There, you choose whether to aid the dragonflight.",sp=0},{t="A Choice Made",b="At another crossroads, Itharius asks you to choose. Then he says your choices so far have been right. What you do now will decide whether they remain so.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Itharius?",a="Through the Oathstone, Itharius speaks into your mind on behalf of Ysera's Dragonflight. He waits in the Swamp of Sorrows, seeking to redeem Eranikus's corrupted soul.",al={"who is itharius","itharius role","who sends the message"}},{q="What is the Chained Essence of Eranikus?",a="The Chained Essence of Eranikus is the gem that chains the part of Eranikus's mind still free. Itharius asks you to give it up as the first sacrifice.",al={"chained essence of eranikus","what is the chained gem","eranikus essence"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="It follows the first step of The Essence of Eranikus, which bears the same name.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous step"}},{q="Where do you take the Oathstone and the essence?",a="Take the Oathstone and the essence to Itharius in the Swamp of Sorrows. There, you choose whether to aid the dragonflight.",al={"where to bring oathstone","where is itharius","hand in location"}}},kw={"chained essence","eranikus","green dragonflight","itharius","oathstone","swamp of sorrows","ysera"},rel={"quest:3512","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Oathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight",["end"]="Itharius",level="55",id=3374},src={"The Essence of Eranikus (2)"}}
E["quest:3512"] = {t="quest",n="In Eranikus' Own Words",z="swampofsorrows",s="Itharius seeks Eranikus' voice through the gem. Eranikus lies between sleep and death, caught in nightmares. The essence you gave is badly tainted, yet hope remains. Itharius sends you to eastern Winterspring.",h="Itharius seeks Eranikus' voice through the gem.",sec={{t="A Voice Across the Nightmare",b="Itharius says Eranikus lies between sleep and death, caught in a weave of nightmares. The essence you gave is badly tainted, yet there may be a way to reach him. To speak through the gem, Itharius sends you to eastern Winterspring to seek one of his mortal allies.",sp=0},{t="The Spiritspeaker",b="Umbranse the Spiritspeaker is the ally Itharius has in mind. Umbranse is a human who acts as a medium for the dead. Eranikus is not truly dead, but Itharius believes Umbranse may still help.",sp=0},{t="Umbranse's Condition",b="Umbranse says Itharius was wise to send you. Eranikus will soon offer counsel in his own words. For now, Umbranse cannot help directly, but will lend skill at death-speaking.\n\nFirst, Umbranse needs help from someone not held back by age. The most potent augury device in Umbranse's keeping was taken against Umbranse's will. Without it, Eranikus cannot be helped.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this journey?",a="Itharius sends you from the Swamp of Sorrows after taking the tainted essence of Eranikus from you.",al={"who gives in eranikus own words","eranikus quest giver"}},{q="Who is Umbranse the Spiritspeaker?",a="Umbranse the Spiritspeaker is a human medium for the dead and one of Itharius' mortal allies. Umbranse is in eastern Winterspring.",al={"who is umbranse","umbranse spiritspeaker lore"}},{q="Is Eranikus considered dead?",a="Eranikus is not truly dead. He lies between sleep and death, caught in a weave of nightmares.",al={"is eranikus dead","eranikus state of being"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the storyline?",a="This follows the second step of The Essence of Eranikus, when you gave Itharius the gem holding what remained of Eranikus' free will.",al={"eranikus quest chain order","what came before in eranikus own words"}}},kw={"eranikus","itharius","nightmare","spiritspeaker","swamp of sorrows","umbranse","winterspring"},rel={"quest:3374","zone:winterspring","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:human"},m={start="Itharius",["end"]="Umbranse the Spiritspeaker",level="55",id=3512},src={"In Eranikus' Own Words"}}
E["quest:698"] = {t="quest",n="Lack of Surplus",z="swampofsorrows",s="Dar needs more sawtooth meat for the eastern beach outpost. Tok'Kar has little time between guard shifts and cooking for the soldiers, so Dar asks you to bring some.",h="Dar needs more sawtooth meat for the eastern beach outpost.",sec={{t="Supplies for the Shore",b="Dar is gathering supplies for the outpost on the eastern beach. Tok'Kar guards the post and cooks for its soldiers, leaving little time for other work. The soldiers enjoy sawtooth meat when they can get it. Dar has not had time to send another shipment.",sp=0},{t="Choosing the Meat",b="Older sawtooths taste better, Dar says, so leave the young ones alone. They need a year or two to reach full size. Bring eight unprepared sawtooth flanks to Tok'Kar in the Swamp of Sorrows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is requesting the sawtooth meat?",a="Dar, who is stocking the outpost on the eastern beach with supplies.",al={"who gives lack of surplus","who starts lack of surplus","dar swamp of sorrows"}},{q="Where is Tok'Kar stationed?",a="Tok'Kar is stationed at the outpost on the eastern beach, in the Swamp of Sorrows. Bring the meat there.",al={"where is tok'kar","tokkar location","tok'kar outpost"}},{q="Why does Tok'Kar need others to bring meat?",a="Guard shifts and cooking for the soldiers leave Tok'Kar little time in the day.",al={"why does tok'kar need meat","why does dar send food"}},{q="Which sawtooths should be hunted?",a="Hunt older sawtooths. The young ones are less tasty and need a year or two to reach full size.",al={"which sawtooths","what sawtooths drop meat","sawtooth flank source"}},{q="How many flanks are needed?",a="Bring Tok'Kar eight unprepared sawtooth flanks.",al={"how many flanks","unprepared sawtooth flank count"}},{q="What comes next in the chain?",a="A second step under the same name follows.",al={"next quest lack of surplus","lack of surplus follow up"}}},kw={"dar","flank","meat","outpost","sawtooth","swamp of sorrows","tok'kar"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","quest:699"},m={start="Dar",["end"]="Tok'Kar",level="40",faction="Horde",id=698},src={"Lack of Surplus"}}
E["quest:699"] = {t="quest",n="Lack of Surplus",z="swampofsorrows",s="Along the coast, Tok'Kar and his soldiers watch for murlocs threatening Stonard. When the force grows too large, they send warning; for now, Tok'Kar asks you to bring six sawtooth snapper claws.",h="Along the coast, Tok'Kar and his soldiers watch for murlocs threatening Stonard.",sec={{t="Weapons for the Coast",b="Tok'Kar and the soldiers guard Stonard from murlocs along the coast. When the force is too large to face, they warn the town. Tok'Kar has little time to rest, so he asks you to help. Properly prepared, sawtooth snapper claws make fine weapons. Bring him six, and he offers one of the outpost's weapons in return, grateful for the meat and company.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for the claws?",a="Tok'Kar, stationed along the coast to protect Stonard, asks you for the claws.",al={"who gives lack of surplus","quest giver","tokkar"}},{q="Why does Tok'Kar need sawtooth snapper claws?",a="Properly prepared sawtooth snapper claws make fine weapons, and Tok'Kar wants six.",al={"why claws","sawtooth snapper purpose","weapon claws"}},{q="What threat is the coastal post watching for?",a="The soldiers watch for murlocs along the coast. They protect Stonard or warn the town if the force is too large.",al={"coastal dangers","murloc attack stonard","what is tokkar watching"}},{q="Where does this lead next?",a="Threat From the Sea follows.",al={"what comes next","next quest","after lack of surplus"}}},kw={"claws","murlocs","sawtooth snapper","stonard","swamp of sorrows","tok'kar"},rel={"subzone:stonard","quest:698","quest:1422","topic:murloc","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Tok'Kar",["end"]="Tok'Kar",level="42",faction="Horde",id=699},src={"Lack of Surplus (2)"}}
E["subzone:broken-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Broken Hall",z="swampofsorrows",s="Beneath the Pool of Tears, Broken Hall lies flooded at the Temple of Atal'Hakkar's outer edge. Ysera and her green dragons dragged the ziggurat beneath the waters, driving the Atal'ai into deeper chambers.",h="Beneath the Pool of Tears, Broken Hall lies flooded at the Temple of Atal'Hakkar's outer edge.",sec={{t="Flooded Threshold",b="Murky swamp water covers the floor of Broken Hall. When the green dragons dragged the Atal'ai ziggurat beneath the Pool of Tears, the outer hall suffered most. Its floor collapsed, and the Atal'ai zealots left the flooded chamber for deeper parts of the temple. You must wade through the ruins before climbing the stairs to the Hall of Masks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Broken Hall?",a="Broken Hall is the outer entry chamber of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, just beyond its submerged entrance beneath the Pool of Tears.",al={"broken hall overview","what is this place","temple entrance hall"}},{q="Why is the Broken Hall flooded and ruined?",a="The green dragonflight shattered Broken Hall when it dragged the temple beneath the marsh waters to stop the summoning of the Blood God Hakkar. The floor broke, and water filled the chamber.",al={"why broken hall wet","why is broken hall submerged","who broke the hall"}},{q="Are there any Atal'ai trolls living in this hall?",a="Broken Hall lies largely abandoned. After the upper temple drowned, the Atal'ai cultists withdrew to drier, more defensible chambers deeper within the complex.",al={"enemies in broken hall","is broken hall empty"}},{q="Where do the stairs in the Broken Hall lead?",a="The stone stairs out of flooded Broken Hall lead directly to the Hall of Masks.",al={"broken hall stairs","broken hall exit","where to go from broken hall"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll who reveres the loa, you see Broken Hall as a grim reminder of the ruin brought upon Atal'ai zealots who defied their kind to serve Hakkar the Soulflayer."},kw={"atal'ai","broken hall","hall of masks","pool of tears","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar"},rel={"subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:hall-of-masks","subzone:pool-of-tears","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:troll"},src={"Broken Hall"}}
E["subzone:fallow-sanctuary"] = {t="subzone",n="Fallow Sanctuary",z="swampofsorrows",s="In the Swamp of Sorrows, Fallow Sanctuary shelters a tribe cut off from the world they knew. The Lost Ones are mutated draenei, driven feral by grief and homesickness.",h="In the Swamp of Sorrows, Fallow Sanctuary shelters a tribe cut off from the world they knew.",sec={{t="A Refuge Lost to Madness",b="Among the sunken trees of the Swamp of Sorrows, the Lost Ones have made Fallow Sanctuary their refuge. Separation from their ancestral world and dark energies deformed them.\n\nSorrow and isolation wore away at the tribe’s sanity. Now they are hostile and feral, attacking outsiders who enter their village.",sp=0},{t="Vanished Leaders",b="Ongeku and Noboru the Cudgel once guided Fallow Sanctuary. Their absence and deaths left the village without its leaders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Fallow Sanctuary?",a="Fallow Sanctuary is a settlement in the Swamp of Sorrows. It is home to the Lost Ones, a heavily mutated branch of draenei who crossed through the Dark Portal.",al={"fallow sanctuary lore","what is this village","lost one camp swamp"}},{q="Why are the Lost Ones here hostile?",a="Grief and homesickness have driven the Lost Ones of Fallow Sanctuary mad. Trapped on Azeroth and cut off from everything they knew, they have become feral and attack outsiders.",al={"why do lost ones attack","are lost ones evil","feral lost ones"}},{q="Who leads the Fallow Sanctuary?",a="Ongeku and Noboru the Cudgel once led the Lost Ones at Fallow Sanctuary. Their disappearance and deaths left the tribe without its leaders.",al={"who runs fallow sanctuary","noboru","ongeku"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see how dark energies can warp living flesh and shatter a fragile mind in the Lost Ones."},kw={"fallow sanctuary","lost ones","noboru the cudgel","ongeku","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Fallow Sanctuary"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-masks"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Masks",z="swampofsorrows",s="In the Hall of Masks, carved skulls loom over a bone-choked trench beneath the Swamp of Sorrows. The chamber marks a threshold to deeper passages in the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",h="In the Hall of Masks, carved skulls loom over a bone-choked trench beneath the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Threshold",b="Past the staircase from the Broken Hall, you reach a central junction in the Sunken Temple. Stylized skull masks line its stone walls. A deep trench choked with discarded bones cuts across the floor, though its purpose remains unknown. From here, passages lead to the Butchery, the Chamber of Blood, and the Den of the Caller.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Hall of Masks located?",a="The Hall of Masks lies inside the Temple of Atal'Hakkar beneath the Pool of Tears in the Swamp of Sorrows. Descend past the Broken Hall near the sunken complex's entrance to reach it.",al={"hall of masks location","where is hall of masks","find hall of masks"}},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Masks?",a="The Hall of Masks takes its name from the massive carved skull masks mounted on its walls. They loom over all who pass through the temple corridors.",al={"hall of masks name meaning","why masks"}},{q="What was the purpose of the trench in the floor?",a="Bones litter the trench, but its exact purpose remains unknown.",al={"why are there bones in the floor","hall of masks bone pit","trench of bones"}},{q="Where do the passages from this hall lead?",a="Passages from the Hall of Masks lead deeper into the temple, toward the Butchery, the Chamber of Blood, and the Den of the Caller.",al={"hall of masks exits","where does hall of masks lead"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can see how far the Atal'ai zealots went in their desperate pursuit of Hakkar the Soulflayer.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can read the Atal'ai's dark practices in the chamber's grim design and bone-filled trench. The trench's precise use remains unknown."},kw={"atal'ai","broken hall","hall of masks","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar"},rel={"subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:broken-hall","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:troll"},src={"Hall of Masks"}}
E["subzone:harborage"] = {t="subzone",n="Harborage",z="swampofsorrows",s="At the northern edge of the Swamp of Sorrows, Harborage shelters exiled Draenor natives who have kept their minds. They seek peace by the water in a harsh wilderness.",h="At the northern edge of the Swamp of Sorrows, Harborage shelters exiled Draenor natives who have kept their...",sec={{t="A Haven in the Mire",b="At the foot of the northern mountains, you find Harborage, a small camp apart from the feral tribes in the nearby waters. Leather shelters and hanging crystals mark this refuge for exiled survivors from Draenor who have kept their minds. Elders like Magtoor guide the community. Together, they watch the wilderness, its native predators, and the feral tribes of their fallen brothers beyond the camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Harborage?",a="Draenor exiles live in Harborage. Though afflicted and changed after crossing into Azeroth, they have kept their minds and culture, unlike the feral tribes elsewhere in the swamp.",al={"harborage residents","who is at harborage","who lives here"}},{q="Why are the people here peaceful while other swamp tribes attack?",a="Harborage's residents kept their sanity and reason despite their physical transformation and displacement. Their kin across the bog lost their minds to isolation and trauma. Here, the exiles joined together to preserve their dignity.",al={"why are they friendly","lost ones friendly","harborage hostile"}},{q="Who leads the Harborage?",a="Respected elders like Magtoor guide the community as it survives in an alien swamp.",al={"harborage leader","magtoor","chief of harborage"}},{q="Where is the Harborage located?",a="Harborage lies against the northern cliffs of the Swamp of Sorrows, just east of the mountain pass to the Redridge Mountains.",al={"harborage location","where is harborage","find harborage"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler leaving Redridge for the dangerous marsh, Harborage is one of the few places in the northern swamp where you can meet people without facing immediate bloodshed.",["faction:Horde"]="Stonard holds much of the Horde's presence in the swamp. Harborage's reclusive survivors keep to themselves rather than take sides in the regional conflicts."},kw={"broken","draenethyst","harborage","lost ones","magtoor","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire"},src={"Harborage"}}
E["subzone:itharius-s-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Itharius's Cave",z="swampofsorrows",s="Green whelps roam the marsh around Itharius's Cave, where Itharius keeps watch. The cave lies among the far southwestern cliffs of the Swamp of Sorrows.",h="Green whelps roam the marsh around Itharius's Cave, where Itharius keeps watch.",sec={{t="A Hermit Among Whelps",b="Green whelps wander the mire outside Itharius's Cave in the southwestern Swamp of Sorrows. Itharius lives in the damp cavern, far from civilization. He appears to be a high elf, a people rarely found alone in these southern swamps. He keeps watch over the young dragonkin as they grow, sharing their remote home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in this cave?",a="Itharius lives in the cave, apart from civilization, and watches over the local dragonkin. He appears to be a high elf.",al={"who is itharius","cave owner","who lives here"}},{q="Where is Itharius's Cave located?",a="Itharius's Cave lies in the far southwestern Swamp of Sorrows, against the mountain ridges south of the main road.",al={"itharius cave location","where is itharius","how to find cave"}},{q="Why are there green whelps outside the cave?",a="Green whelps live in the surrounding marsh. Itharius watches over and protects the unruly young dragons as they grow.",al={"why whelps here","green dragons swamp of sorrows","whelps outside"}},{q="Why would a high elf live out in the swamp?",a="Itharius appears to be a high elf, a people rarely seen in these southern bogs. He remains in the swamp to safeguard its green dragonkin, living alone in his remote den.",al={"high elf in swamp","why is itharius here"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Green dragonkin in the swamp may interest you as a druid. Your traditions are tied to the Green Dragonflight and the Emerald Dream."},kw={"dragonkin","green whelps","high elf","itharius","itharius's cave","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Itharius's Cave"}}
E["subzone:misty-reed-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Reed Post",z="swampofsorrows",s="Between Stagalbog and the Misty Reed Strand, Misty Reed Post keeps watch over the wetlands and the dangerous coast. The Horde holds this camp under Stonard's authority.",h="Between Stagalbog and the Misty Reed Strand, Misty Reed Post keeps watch over the wetlands and the dangerous...",sec={{t="A Lonely Outpost",b="A handful of Stonard hunters, the shaman Katar, and Tok'Kar keep watch between Stagalbog and the eastern shore. The camp stands under Stonard's banner, exposed to marsh wildlife and lingering damp. Tok'Kar hopes Horde command in Stonard will send an orcish burrow or watchtower. For now, the scouts hold the marsh with tents, campfire smoke, and sharpened steel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Misty Reed Post?",a="Misty Reed Post is a forward camp for the Horde garrison at Stonard. Its sentries watch the coast and the swamp beasts between Stagalbog and the Misty Reed Strand.",al={"why is misty reed post here","misty reed post purpose","what is this camp"}},{q="Who is in charge here?",a="Tok'Kar leads Misty Reed Post with Katar, a Stonard shaman, and several Stonard hunters. He hopes the camp will receive resources for permanent fortifications.",al={"who leads misty reed post","tokkar","tok'kar"}},{q="Is there a flight master at Misty Reed Post?",a="No. Misty Reed Post has no wind rider facilities. Follow the road west to Stonard for flight paths.",al={"misty reed flight path","is there a flight path here","flight master misty reed post"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find shelter and local guidance here while scouting the marsh's dangerous eastern edge.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you share this post with Stonard hunters who know the surrounding marsh. Their work calls for grit as they track and survive its hostile wetland predators."},kw={"katar","misty reed post","misty reed strand","stagalbog","stonard","swamp of sorrows","tok'kar"},rel={"subzone:stonard","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:misty-reed-strand","subzone:stagalbog","topic:horde"},src={"Misty Reed Post"}}
E["subzone:misty-reed-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Reed Strand",z="swampofsorrows",s="At Misty Reed Strand, the Great Sea meets the eastern edge of the Swamp of Sorrows. Crabs, crocolisks, and murlocs contest its foggy shore, where driftwood and wreckage wash ashore.",h="At Misty Reed Strand, the Great Sea meets the eastern edge of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Foggy Shoreline",b="Fog rolls in from the Great Sea along Misty Reed Strand, the eastern edge of the Swamp of Sorrows. It hides the water and dulls the cries of wildlife. Driftwood, sea debris, and rotting plants from the inland bog litter the beach. No permanent settlement holds this remote shore. Aggressive crabs forage among the debris, crocolisks stalk the water’s edge, and territorial murlocs defend their grounds.",sp=0},{t="Contested Waters",b="Neither the Alliance nor the Horde claims the beach, though scouts from both send adventurers there. Alliance parties gather driftwood and salvage while thinning the crab population. Farther inland, Horde outposts watch the murloc camps. They send fighters to curb the tribes before raiders push toward Stonard or threaten travel through the marsh.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Misty Reed Strand located?",a="Misty Reed Strand runs along the far eastern edge of the Swamp of Sorrows, beside the Great Sea. You can reach it by traveling east through the wetlands from Stonard or along the marsh paths surrounding it.",al={"where is misty reed strand","misty reed strand location","how to get to misty reed strand"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the strand?",a="Giant coastal crabs, swamp crocolisks, and hostile murloc tribes inhabit the shoreline, scavenging along the tide lines.",al={"monsters at misty reed strand","what lives on misty reed strand","misty reed strand enemies"}},{q="Are there any settlements on the beach?",a="No permanent friendly town or established military outpost stands on the beach. The nearest settlements lie farther inland in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"towns near misty reed strand","misty reed strand base","friendly camps misty reed strand"}},{q="Why do the factions send adventurers to the Misty Reed Strand?",a="The Alliance sends parties to gather driftwood and coastal salvage, while Horde outposts send fighters to curb the murloc tribes along the surf.",al={"why go to misty reed strand","misty reed strand quests"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts traveling south from Nethergarde or through the marshlands scavenge driftwood and other resources on the beach. They also keep its aggressive wildlife at bay.",["faction:Horde"]="Stonard's defenders see the strand's murloc tribes as an unmanaged threat. They often order combat patrols to clear the encampments along the surf."},kw={"beach","coast","crocolisk","driftwood","great sea","misty reed strand","murloc","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Misty Reed Strand"}}
E["subzone:misty-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Valley",z="swampofsorrows",s="Fog gathers in Misty Valley, north of the pass into Deadwind. Swamp beasts and marsh horrors roam its secluded basin in the northwestern Swamp of Sorrows.",h="Fog gathers in Misty Valley, north of the pass into Deadwind.",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Glen",b="Cliffs rise between the Swamp of Sorrows and Deadwind Pass, and fog shrouds the hollow below. Colossal marsh elementals crowd this isolated valley. Swampwalkers and ancient swampwalker elders roam among creeping tangled horrors. At the gorge’s far end, a cavern shelters one of the bog’s strongest natural threats: the Mire Lord.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Misty Valley located?",a="Misty Valley lies in the far northwestern Swamp of Sorrows, directly north of the road into Deadwind Pass.",al={"misty valley location","where is misty valley","misty valley swamp of sorrows"}},{q="What creatures inhabit this valley?",a="Swampwalkers, elder swampwalkers, and tangled horrors roam the fog.",al={"misty valley mobs","what lives in misty valley","enemies in misty valley"}},{q="What is inside the cave at the back of the valley?",a="The Mire Lord dwells deep inside the cave at Misty Valley’s rear. This massive, powerful marsh elemental reigns over the secluded hollow.",al={"misty valley cave","mire lord cave","who is in misty valley cave"}},{q="Is the Misty Valley safe to traverse?",a="Misty Valley is dangerous to cross. Towering swampwalkers and tangled horrors roam its dense fog, hostile to travelers who leave the main road.",al={"is misty valley dangerous","misty valley level"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see swampwalkers and tangled horrors as the wild fury of marsh elementals, bound to the swamp’s primordial nature."},kw={"deadwind pass","mire lord","misty valley","swamp of sorrows","swampwalker","tangled horror"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:deadwind"},src={"Misty Valley"}}
E["subzone:pool-of-tears"] = {t="subzone",n="Pool of Tears",z="swampofsorrows",s="In the eastern Swamp of Sorrows, the Pool of Tears surrounds a sunken temple. Frenzies patrol its murky waters, and troll ruins line its drowned banks.",h="In the eastern Swamp of Sorrows, the Pool of Tears surrounds a sunken temple.",sec={{t="A Drowned Sanctuary",b="Atal'ai trolls raised a great ziggurat to Hakkar the Soulflayer, their bloodthirsty god. Ysera, the Dragon Aspect, was horrified by the blasphemies within. She broke the ground beneath the temple and sank it into the marsh. Water covered the ruins, but the ziggurat still lies beneath silt and lake water. Green drakes keep watch nearby, guarding against the corruption sealed below.",sp=0},{t="Waters of Peril",b="Crossing the murky lake toward the sunken halls is perilous. Flesh-eating frenzies haunt the water, while Atal'ai artifacts and drowned stonework lie across the muddy floor. To reach the temple's upper passages, you must brave the hostile shallows. There, cultists and lingering dragon guardians struggle for control of the dark sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Pool of Tears?",a="No record tells why the lake is called the Pool of Tears. It is known for the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, which Ysera sank beneath its waters to stop Hakkar's summoning.",al={"pool of tears name origin","why pool of tears","pool of tears meaning"}},{q="What is the massive building in the center of the lake?",a="The massive building in the lake is the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, often called the Sunken Temple. Once a towering Atal'ai ziggurat, it was sunk beneath the water by Ysera and remains partly submerged at the pool's center.",al={"building in pool of tears","ruins in lake swamp of sorrows","sunken temple location"}},{q="Why are there green dragons around the water?",a="Ysera's brood came to destroy the temple and drown its vile ceremonies. Green drakes and dragonkin still watch the lake, keeping the Atal'ai cultists from completing their summoning of the Blood God.",al={"green dragons swamp of sorrows","why are dragons here","ysera temple lake"}},{q="Is it safe to swim across the pool?",a="No. Aggressive, flesh-eating frenzies infest the lake and attack anyone swimming toward the temple entrance.",al={"pool of tears swimming","sharks in pool of tears","frenzies swamp of sorrows"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can see the pool as a grim warning of what follows when trollkind embraces forbidden blood magic like that of the Atal'ai.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can honor the lake as the place where Ysera and the Green Dragonflight intervened to stem the Blood God's taint."},kw={"atal'ai","frenzies","pool of tears","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar","ysera"},rel={"subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Pool of Tears"}}
E["subzone:shifting-mire"] = {t="subzone",n="Shifting Mire",z="swampofsorrows",s="In the Swamp of Sorrows, the Shifting Mire spreads west of the Pool of Tears. Beneath its murky water, strange silt drifts and gathers under an unseen force.",h="In the Swamp of Sorrows, the Shifting Mire spreads west of the Pool of Tears.",sec={{t="A Living Bog",b="The Shifting Mire covers the swamp’s central reaches, where firm ground is scarce. Along the bog floor, fine silt shifts and gathers under a strange energy in the peat. Predators prowl the drifting mud: swamp jaguars, massive sorrow spinners, and hungry sawtooth crocolisks. Bands of broken draenei called the Lost Ones stalk the sunken paths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Shifting Mire?",a="Fine silt gives the Shifting Mire its name. A mysterious current of energy makes the mud gather, drift, and flow across the wetlands instead of settling.",al={"shifting mire name origin","why shifting mire","why does the ground move"}},{q="What creatures live in the Shifting Mire?",a="Sawtooth crocolisks lurk in the shallows, while giant sorrow spinners weave webs in the boughs. Swamp jaguars pass unseen through the mire, and roaming Lost Ones frequent the area. The Lost Ones are draenei warped and exiled from their homeworld.",al={"shifting mire mobs","what is in shifting mire"}},{q="Where is the Shifting Mire located?",a="The Shifting Mire covers the central expanse of the Swamp of Sorrows, directly west of the Pool of Tears.",al={"shifting mire location","where is shifting mire"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, track carefully through tangled brush and drifting water. Stay alert for stealthy swamp jaguars and venomous sorrow spinners hidden in the foliage."},kw={"crocolisks","jaguars","lost ones","shifting mire","silt","sorrow spinners","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:pool-of-tears"},src={"Shifting Mire"}}
E["subzone:sorrowmurk"] = {t="subzone",n="Sorrowmurk",z="swampofsorrows",s="Green dragonkin guard the way to the Sunken Temple in Sorrowmurk. East of the Pool of Tears, this wetland remains one of the most perilous reaches of the eastern marshes.",h="Green dragonkin guard the way to the Sunken Temple in Sorrowmurk.",sec={{t="A Perilous Border",b="Along the eastern edge of the Pool of Tears, you reach Sorrowmurk where the mire meets the Forbidding Sea. Green dragonspawn and towering drakes patrol its waters and tangled boughs. They are remnants of the brood sent to watch over the submerged Temple of Atal'Hakkar. Their presence makes these sodden reaches perilous for any traveler.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Sorrowmurk located?",a="Sorrowmurk lies along the coast in the easternmost Swamp of Sorrows, beyond the Pool of Tears and the sunken ruins of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",al={"sorrowmurk location","where is sorrowmurk","sorrowmurk map"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Sorrowmurk?",a="Green dragonkin inhabit Sorrowmurk. Aggressive dragonspawn and large drakes patrol the marsh around the temple waters.",al={"sorrowmurk mobs","what lives in sorrowmurk","sorrowmurk enemies"}},{q="Why are there green dragons in the Sorrowmurk?",a="Ysera tasked the Green Dragonflight with watching over the Pool of Tears and keeping the evil sunken within the Temple of Atal'Hakkar contained.",al={"why dragons here","green dragonflight swamp of sorrows","temple dragons"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may find the green dragonkin here a tragic sight. Corruption touches the Emerald Dream's guardians in these wetlands."},kw={"atal'hakkar","dragonspawn","green dragonflight","green drake","pool of tears","sorrowmurk","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:pool-of-tears"},src={"Sorrowmurk"}}
E["subzone:splinterspear-junction"] = {t="subzone",n="Splinterspear Junction",z="swampofsorrows",s="Horde sentries hold Splinterspear Junction where the Swamp of Sorrows road forks. North lies the Harborage and Fallow Sanctuary; south, the road passes Stonard toward the Blasted Lands.",h="Horde sentries hold Splinterspear Junction where the Swamp of Sorrows road forks.",sec={{t="A Crossroads of Conflict",b="At Splinterspear Junction, the road through the Swamp of Sorrows divides. The northern trail leads toward the Lost One refuge of the Harborage and the Fallow Sanctuary. South, the road passes Stonard on its way to the Blasted Lands.\n\nAn ancient orcish watchtower overlooks the fork. Horde troops hold it and patrol the roads. For Horde travelers, the tower offers a secure point in a treacherous marsh. For Alliance travelers, it is a deadly ambush on an unforgiving trail.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the roads at Splinterspear Junction lead?",a="North, the fork leads toward the Lost One refuge of the Harborage and the Fallow Sanctuary. South, the road passes Stonard and continues to the Blasted Lands.",al={"where does the road go","splinterspear paths","which way at splinterspear"}},{q="Is Splinterspear Junction safe for Alliance travelers?",a="No. Horde troops hold the junction, garrison its watchtower, and patrol the roads. Openly hostile to the Alliance, they attack passing adventurers on sight.",al={"alliance safe splinterspear","are guards hostile","splinterspear pvp"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, watch your step at Splinterspear Junction. Horde sentries guard the orcish watchtower and are eager to cut down intruders straying from Darkshire.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, use the watchtower at Splinterspear Junction as a vital waypoint and security checkpoint on the road between Stonard and northern destinations in the swamp."},kw={"harborage","splinterspear junction","stonard","swamp of sorrows","watchtower"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:stonard","subzone:harborage","subzone:fallow-sanctuary","zone:blastedlands","topic:horde"},src={"Splinterspear Junction"}}
E["subzone:stagalbog"] = {t="subzone",n="Stagalbog",z="swampofsorrows",s="Along the southern mountains, Stagalbog remains an untamed stretch of marsh, south of the Pool of Tears.",h="Along the southern mountains, Stagalbog remains an untamed stretch of marsh, south of the Pool of Tears.",sec={{t="The Southern Mire",b="Below the southern crags, stagnant water gathers among drooping reeds and tangled growth. The tainted Pool of Tears borders Stagalbog to the north, with the sunken ruins of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar just beyond. Rough wildlife roams the mire, where civilization has made no foothold.",sp=0},{t="Shadow of the Temple",b="Beside the Pool of Tears, Stagalbog lies under the shadows and corruption seeping from the Sunken Temple.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Stagalbog located?",a="Stagalbog lies in the southern Swamp of Sorrows, directly south of the Pool of Tears along the base of the southern mountain range.",al={"stagalbog location","where is stagalbog","how to find stagalbog"}},{q="What threats can be found wandering the bog?",a="Native marsh beasts and predatory creatures roam the bog.",al={"stagalbog mobs","monsters in stagalbog"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Damp, shaded roots in Stagalbog provide prime growing conditions for swamp flora that thrive away from trodden paths.",["class:Hunter"]="Between the marsh water and mountain cliffs, Stagalbog's quiet stretches give native swamp beasts room to roam."},kw={"marsh","pool of tears","stagalbog","stagalbog cave","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:stagalbog-cave","subzone:pool-of-tears","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar"},src={"Stagalbog"}}
E["subzone:stagalbog-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Stagalbog Cave",z="swampofsorrows",s="Marsh murlocs shelter in Stagalbog Cave, deep in the eastern Swamp of Sorrows.",h="Marsh murlocs shelter in Stagalbog Cave, deep in the eastern Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="Den of the Marsh Tribe",b="In the eastern Swamp of Sorrows, the Marsh murlocs shelter from the rain in Stagalbog Cave. They guard its winding chambers under their chief mystic, the Swamp Talker. Near the sunken mire of the Stagalbog, their gurgling calls cross the mossy banks and warn travelers away from their nesting grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Stagalbog Cave?",a="Stagalbog Cave lies in the Stagalbog, in the eastern Swamp of Sorrows. Marsh murlocs occupy the natural cavern.",al={"where is stagalbog cave","what's in stagalbog cave"}},{q="Who rules the cave?",a="The Marsh tribe rules the cave under the Swamp Talker. The murloc mystic oversees their rituals and defenses in its damp chambers.",al={"stagalbog boss","swamp talker","who leads the murlocs here"}},{q="Are there friendly settlements nearby?",a="Hostile marshlands surround the cave. For the Horde, the nearest friendly settlement is Stonard, to the west.",al={"nearest town","vendors near stagalbog"}}},kw={"marsh murlocs","murloc den","stagalbog","stagalbog cave","swamp of sorrows","swamp talker"},rel={"subzone:stagalbog","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc"},src={"Stagalbog Cave"}}
E["subzone:stonard"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonard",z="swampofsorrows",s="In the southern Swamp of Sorrows, Stonard holds a fortified Horde foothold. The outpost dates to the First War and watches the Blasted Lands from the marsh.",h="In the southern Swamp of Sorrows, Stonard holds a fortified Horde foothold.",sec={{t="A Relic of the First War",b="Stonard began as an Old Horde post in the marsh beyond the Dark Portal. When the invaders crossed into what was then the Black Morass, Stonard and Rockard anchored their lines. Both posts were damaged and abandoned after the Second War. Thrall's New Horde rebuilt Stonard and placed a garrison there. Its Great Hall and fortified burrows now hold a Horde presence amid the dangerous swamp.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Outpost",b="Scouts and cartographers range from Stonard into the surrounding swamp. They chart its waters and watch for hostile beasts, lost draenei wanderers, and the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar to the east. North of the shattered Blasted Lands, the outpost also gives the Horde a staging ground. The dormant Dark Portal remains under watch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Stonard important to the Horde?",a="Stonard gives the Horde a fortified base in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. Its scouts chart the dangerous Swamp of Sorrows, and its garrison provides a staging ground for assaults on the nearby Sunken Temple. The outpost also keeps Horde forces close to the Blasted Lands.",al={"why is stonard here","stonard purpose","what is stonard"}},{q="How old is Stonard?",a="Stonard dates to the First War, when the Old Horde founded it after crossing the Dark Portal. The outpost fell into disuse after the Second War. Thrall's New Horde later rebuilt it.",al={"stonard history","when was stonard built","who founded stonard"}},{q="What happened to its sister settlement, Rockard?",a="Rockard was founded alongside Stonard during the First War, and together the posts anchored the Old Horde's lines in the swamp. The New Horde rebuilt Stonard, but Rockard's fate since the wars is not recorded.",al={"what is rockard","rockard history","stonard sister town"}},{q="Can you fly or travel directly to Stonard?",a="Yes. Stonard's flight paths connect it to Kargath, Flame Crest, Grom'gol Base Camp, Booty Bay, and Rog'mar in the Riverglades.",al={"stonard flight path","how to get to stonard","stonard portals"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can find guidance and training at Stonard, a Horde shaman enclave in the southern Eastern Kingdoms, far from Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Stonard as your fortified outpost between the Badlands to the north and Stranglethorn Vale to the west."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","great hall","orcs","rockard","stonard","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:blastedlands","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:dark-portal","subzone:kargath","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","topic:old-horde","topic:new-horde"},src={"Stonard"}}
E["subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar"] = {t="subzone",n="Temple of Atal'Hakkar",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Temple of Atal'Hakkar lies drowned beneath the Swamp of Sorrows, its halls still touched by corruption. Exiled troll priests raised it for Hakkar, and Ysera's green dragons sank it beneath the marsh centuries ago.",h="The Temple of Atal'Hakkar lies drowned beneath the Swamp of Sorrows, its halls still touched by corruption.",sec={{t="Wrath of the Green Flight",b="More than a thousand years ago, civil war broke the Gurubashi Empire after the Atal'ai priesthood tried to summon Hakkar the Soulflayer. Exiled north, the surviving priests built a great stone temple in the Swamp of Sorrows to finish their work. Ysera, the Dragon Aspect, learned of their scheme and drove the temple deep into the mire. Its halls flooded beneath the Pool of Tears, while green dragon wardens remained to guard the ruins and keep Hakkar from returning.",sp=0},{t="A Slumber Turned Nightmare",b="The flooded halls gave the Atal'ai the seclusion to continue their sacrifices. Over the centuries, corruption took hold of the guardians. The green dragon sentinels fell into madness, while the Atal'ai, led by Jammal'an the Prophet, prepare the way for Hakkar's avatar. The Horde and Alliance watch the sunken temple uneasily as rumors rise from the swamp's depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the temple underwater?",a="Ysera, Aspect of the green dragonflight, sank the temple beneath the marsh waters to stop the Atal'ai trolls from summoning the blood god Hakkar into Azeroth.",al={"why sunken temple","who sunk the temple","how did it sink"}},{q="Who are the Atal'ai?",a="The Atal'ai are fanatical troll priests exiled from the southern Gurubashi Empire for practicing blood magic and trying to bring Hakkar the Soulflayer into the physical realm.",al={"atalai lore","who built the sunken temple","atal'ai priests"}},{q="Why are there green dragons here?",a="Ysera sent green dragons as guardians to watch the sunken ruins, keep trespassers out, and prevent Hakkar's summoning. Many have fallen to madness and dark corruption.",al={"why dragons in swamp","green dragonflight sunken temple"}},{q="How do you get inside the temple?",a="Swim into the flooded ruins from the Pool of Tears and pass through the submerged ways of the Broken Hall. Then climb the stone corridors, including the Hall of Masks.",al={"how to enter sunken temple","sunken temple entrance","getting into atal hakkar"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you see these ruins as a grim reminder of the blood-soaked madness that ruined the ancient Gurubashi Empire and the lasting danger of Hakkar the Soulflayer.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know corruption among Ysera's green dragon wardens strikes at the heart of the Emerald Dream. The depths demand swift investigation."},kw={"atal'ai","atal'hakkar","eranikus","hakkar","jammal'an","pool of tears","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","ysera"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:pool-of-tears","subzone:broken-hall","subzone:hall-of-masks","topic:troll","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:explorers-league","npc:thrall"},src={"Temple of Atal'Hakkar"}}
E["zone:swampofsorrows"] = {t="zone",n="Swamp of Sorrows",z="swampofsorrows",s="Green dragonspawn guard the drowned Temple of Atal'Hakkar beneath the Pool of Tears. Between Deadwind Pass and the Blasted Lands, this salt-crusted mire holds dangerous wildlife and the Horde garrison at Stonard. The Alliance has no safe haven here.",h="Green dragonspawn guard the drowned Temple of Atal'Hakkar beneath the Pool of Tears.",sec={{t="A Drowned History",b="The Swamp of Sorrows was once the northern half of the vast Black Morass. After the Gurubashi Empire shattered, fanatical Atal'ai trolls fled into the mire and built the Temple of Atal'Hakkar. They meant to summon Hakkar the Soulflayer, their bloodthirsty loa. The Aspect Ysera sensed the danger and drowned the cursed pyramid beneath the Pool of Tears. Green dragonflight guardians led by Eranikus were set to watch over it.\n\nLater, the Dark Portal's cataclysm scorched the southern morass into the Blasted Lands. The northern fen took its sorrowful name.",sp=0},{t="Outposts and Broken Exiles",b="Stonard is the swamp's main foothold for settled folk. First established during the First War alongside Rockard and Kyross, both now ruined, it was rebuilt under Thrall as the Horde's southernmost staging ground in the Eastern Kingdoms.\n\nStrange wanderers cross the fen beyond its palisades. Draenei stranded on Azeroth grew homesick and mad, becoming feral Lost Ones. At the Harborage, a small enclave of lucid Broken exiles remains wary, yet willing to trade peacefully with travelers.",sp=0},{t="The Sinking Mire",b="Predators make every crossing of the Swamp of Sorrows dangerous. Deep bogs conceal lunging crocolisks, venomous spiders, prowling swamp jaguars, and bog beasts coated in marsh debris. Vicious murlocs crawl through coastal caverns and along the Misty Reed Strand.\n\nSalt-laden tides creep inland and crust rotten logs with brine. Farther east, aggressive elite dragonspawn guard the approaches to the Sunken Temple in Sorrowmurk. They attack anyone who strays near their vigil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I reach the Swamp of Sorrows?",a="The common overland route runs east from Darkshire in Duskwood, through haunted Deadwind Pass, and down into the marsh. From the south, follow the main road north out of the Blasted Lands.",al={"how to get to swamp of sorrows","swamp of sorrows road","getting to stonard"}},{q="Why is the Temple of Atal'Hakkar underwater?",a="Centuries ago, the Atal'ai priesthood tried to summon Hakkar the Soulflayer into Azeroth. Ysera, Aspect of the Green Flight, discovered their demonic blood rites and drowned the temple in the bog to avert disaster. Green dragonspawn guard its submerged halls.",al={"why is sunken temple sunk","who sank the temple","sunken temple lore"}},{q="What is Stonard?",a="Stonard began as one of the Orcish Horde's first settlements after it crossed the Dark Portal during the First War. Fighting ravaged the outpost, but Thrall recently ordered it reclaimed and rebuilt to anchor Horde logistics near the Blasted Lands.",al={"stonard history","orc base in swamp","who built stonard"}},{q="Are there any Alliance settlements here?",a="The Swamp of Sorrows has no Alliance settlements, guards, or flight paths. If you travel through the mire, base yourself in Darkshire to the west or Nethergarde Keep to the south.",al={"alliance base swamp of sorrows","alliance flight path swamp","where is alliance camp"}},{q="Who are the strange mutated humanoids in the swamp?",a="These strange humanoids are draenei stranded on Azeroth after the Dark Portal collapsed. Cut off from their world, most fell to despair and madness and became hostile Lost Ones. A small group of sane Broken exiles found refuge at the Harborage in the northwest, choosing neutral survival over mindless rage.",al={"who are the lost ones","what is the harborage","draenei in swamp"}},{q="What is Sorrowmurk?",a="Sorrowmurk is the dense marshland east of the Pool of Tears. Elite green dragonspawn and whelps patrol there, violently turning mortals away to protect the secrets of the Sunken Temple.",al={"dragon area swamp of sorrows","sorrowmurk dragons","green dragonspawn swamp"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Stonard is your vital forward redoubt in the southern continent. Wyvern routes connect it directly to Kargath, Flame Crest, Grom'gol Base Camp, Booty Bay, and Rog'mar in the Riverglades.",["faction:Alliance"]="With no outpost to rally behind, you face an isolated, hostile journey through the swamp. Prepare carefully in Darkshire or Nethergarde Keep before setting out.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The marsh is one of Azeroth's few rich sources of blindweed. You can also find plenty of liferoot, fadeleaf, and stranglekelp.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Along the mountainous crags on the swamp's northern and southern edges, you can gather iron, gold, mithril, and truesilver.",["race:Troll"]="The sunken ruins of Atal'Hakkar recall the dark blood magic that fractured the Gurubashi Empire and drew the Dragon Aspects' wrath."},kw={"black morass","broken","harborage","lost ones","pool of tears","sorrowmurk","stonard","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar"},rel={"subzone:stonard","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:pool-of-tears","subzone:harborage","subzone:sorrowmurk","zone:blastedlands","npc:fel-zerul"},src={"Swamp of Sorrows (Classic)","Swamp of Sorrows"}}
